            "id": "S59_G",
            "passage": "It started with one message.\n\nNina received it on the class chat group on a Monday morning: a photo of her, taken at Sports Day, with a caption that made fun of the way she ran. She did not know who sent it — the account used a fake name she did not recognise.\n\nBy lunchtime, twelve people laughed at it.\n\nNina did not go to the canteen that day. She sat at her desk and stared at her pencil case.\n\nHer form teacher, Mrs Tan, noticed. At the end of the day, she asked Nina to stay behind.\n\n'I didn't want to make a fuss,' Nina said.\n\nMrs Tan sat down across from her. 'Making a fuss,' she said quietly, 'is exactly what we need to do when something like this happens. Not to punish. To fix.'\n\nNina showed her the screenshot. Mrs Tan took her time looking at it, then nodded.\n\n'This is not a joke,' she said. 'It is not harmless. And it is not going to continue.'\n\nBy the next morning, the post was removed and the fake account was reported. Nina did not know what the school said to the students involved. But the laughing stopped.",
